Legacy CBC checks padding rather than authenticating the password. A random
salt can give this wrong key valid padding. Keep this error-path fixture
deterministic while running the real encryption and decryption operations.

https://github.com/fastlane/fastlane/issues/21663

--- a/match/spec/encryption/openssl_spec.rb
+++ b/match/spec/encryption/openssl_spec.rb
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
     end
 
     it "raises an exception if invalid password is passed" do
+      # Keep the legacy CBC error-path fixture deterministic.
+      allow(SecureRandom).to receive(:random_bytes).with(8).and_return("\0" * 8)
       @e.encrypt_files
       expect(File.read(@full_path)).to_not(eq(@content))
 
